I posted the follwing message and attachment a few weeks ago but it
seems to me it got somehow lost on the way. So I simply post it again:
> A long time ago I wrote:
> > I guess I=92ll update the wiki page with all the suggestions you made.
>=20
> So I finally did it. The reason I took so long was that I forgot
> it. :D I applied tsani=92s suggestions. I also cleaned the page up a
> bit. I *think* I am quite happy with the list now.
>=20
> I also created a CSV file with definitions for the dictionary in
> Lojban, English and German. I *hope* it=92s an useful format for the
> jbovlaste admin(s). Other languages could easily be added
> with your favourite spreadsheet software. Well, as long as you don=92t
> use a comma in the text ;-). You find this file attached to this
> e-mail.
>=20
> The CSV file is UTF-8 encoded, the delimeter character is the comma.
> The first line is the caption line.
>=20
> But before anyone considers to apply the list to jbovlaste, please
> check it for errors or give your comments if you don=92t like
> this-or-that. But I *think* it=92s error-free.

Context: This is about the invention of a bunch of zi'evla for selma'o
names. =93BAI=94 would be =93cmavrbai=94 in Lojban, for example. This was
discussed on the mailing list before. The valsi are documentated here:
<http://mw.lojban.org/index.php/selma%27o_zi%27evla>
Note that the wiki page also includes things like =93cmavrko'axipa=94 (for
=93KOhA1=94). Ignore this part of the page for the moment, it is still
half-baked (but reviews are welcome!). They aren=92t included in the CSV
file. The other words should be stable IMO.

I wish to have the selma'o zi'evla appear in jbovlaste (see CSV). It
would be a pain in the ass to enter those manually. Otherwise all the
work of me and others would be void. But I wish this only if there are
no more serious flaws, of course. Please check. But I hope all flaws
should have been addressed and fixed now.

